A representative SEM image of the ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane prepared by in situ hydrothermal growth is shown in Figure 2a. Well-intergrown LDH crystallites with no conspicuous cracks on the membrane surface could be clearly observed. A cross-sectional image showed that the ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane was uniform with a thickness of approximately \(2.5\;\upmu\mathrm{m}\) (Figure 2b). The XRD pattern (Figure 3b) showed two conspicuous diffraction peaks at \(2\theta\) of \(9.8^{\circ}\) and \(19.8^{\circ}\), which could be assigned to the (003) and (006) reflection planes of the LDH phase. The \(d_{(003)}\)-spacing was calculated, according to the Bragg equation, to be \(9.0\;\mathrm{\AA}\), which corresponded to the basal spacing of LDHs and coincided with reports on LDHs intercalated with nitrate anions.[24]

