Compared with the pure \(\mathrm{ZnAl-NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane, the \(\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) SF and \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\) permeance increased by about 5 and 2 times, respectively, on the ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membranes at \(90\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\). This result was reasonable, as partial dissolution of the \(\mathrm{ZnAl-NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane indeed led to a reduced diffusion barrier. Furthermore, the \(\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) SF and \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\) permeance on the ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membrane even surpassed those on the \(\mathrm{NiAl-}\mathrm{CO}_{3}\) LDH (gallery height: \(0.32\;\mathrm{nm}\)) and ZIF-8 membranes (Figure S4) under the given conditions.[26] It should be noted that the ZIF-8 membrane used as a reference was prepared by the liquid-phase epitaxy (LPE) method, because both membrane fabrication processes were similar \((\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\) ions were gradually released to the bulk solution), and both ZIF-8 membranes had similar grain size and membrane thickness. Apart from the separation of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}\), we found that \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) SF on the ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membrane also reached 12.9. This value was considerably higher than most reported for MOF and LDH membranes.[30]

A further increase in the operating temperature resulted in the reduction of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) SF to a certain extent; however, both the SF and \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\) permeance remained considerably higher than those on the pure \(\mathrm{ZnAl-NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane (Figure S5). Finally, the thermal stability of the ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membrane was tested for the separation of an equimolecular mixture of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\) and \(\mathrm{CH}_{4}\). Both the \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\) permeance and \(\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) SF were unchanged for at least \(30\,\mathrm{h}\) (Figure S6). Considering the high chemical flexibility of both LDHs and MOFs, we firmly believe that MOF-LDH composite membranes prepared in this way hold great potential for further performance improvements.

Very recently we demonstrated that the surface modification of substrates with \(\mathrm{ZnAl-}\mathrm{CO}_{3}\) LDH buffer layers enabled a great enhancement of the heterogeneous nucleation of ZIF-8 crystals and resulted in the formation of \(20\;\upmu\mathrm{m}\) thick ZIF-8 membranes.[31] Nevertheless, the \(\mathrm{ZnAl-}\mathrm{CO}_{3}\) LDH buffer layer neither served as the \(\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\) source of the ZIF-8 phase nor did it lead to an enhanced gas selectivity. In contrast, in the present study the prepared ZIF-8 top layer had a thickness of merely \(1.1\;\upmu\mathrm{m}\). Moreover, the \(\mathrm{ZnAl-NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane served as the \(\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\) source of the ZIF-8 layer and greatly contributed to the enhancement of gas selectivity.

In summary, we successfully prepared high-quality ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membranes by a partial selfconversion of laminated membranes to MOFs. First ZnAl\(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH membranes, which also served as the \(\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\) source for ZIF-8, were grown in situ on the \(\gamma\!-\!\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}\) substrate. Subsequent solvothermal treatment of LDH membranes in methanol containing 2-mIm led to a partial dissolution of the \(\mathrm{ZnAl-NO}_{3}\) LDH layers and the final formation of ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membranes, which showed remarkably enhanced mixed \(\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) gas selectivity and \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\)

permeance. This post-synthetic partial conversion of a laminated membrane to a MOF layer paves a new avenue for designing and fabricating high-performance gas-separation membranes.

# Experimental Section

Preparation of the \(\mathrm{ZnAl-NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane: The asymmetric porous \(\alpha\mathrm{{-}}\mathrm{{Al}}_{2}\mathrm{{O}}_{3}\) substrate was supplied by Fraunhofer IKTS. Its diameter and thickness were \(10\;\mathrm{mm}\) and \(1\;\mathrm{mm}\), respectively. Before in situ growth, a \(\gamma\!-\!\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}\) intermediate layer was dip-coated on the substrate.[32]

The precursor solution was prepared by dissolving Zn\((\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\,\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) \((98.0\;\mathrm{wt.}\%\) , Sigma–Aldrich, \(5.8\;\mathrm{g}\) ), \(\mathrm{NH}_{4}\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) \((98.0\;\mathrm{wt.}\%\) , Aldrich, \(4.8\;\mathrm{g}\) ), and glycine (sodium salt, \(98.0\;\mathrm{wt.}\%\) , Acros, \(0.8\;\mathrm{g}\) ) into double deionized water \(\mathrm{[00\,mL]}\) ). Then \(\mathrm{NH}_{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) (1 wt. \(\%\) , Aldrich, \(10\;\mathrm{mL}\) ) was added dropwise over \(10\;\mathrm{min}\) to the aqueous solution under stirring in an ice bath. Consequently the \(\gamma\!-\!\mathrm{Al}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}\) -modified alumina substrates were placed vertically into a \(50\;\mathrm{mL}\) Teflon-lined stainless-steel vessel. Next, precursor solution \((35\;\mathrm{mL})\) was poured into the vessel, which was then sealed. The vessel was put into a convection oven preheated at \(65\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\). After \(40\,\mathrm{h}\), the membrane was removed, washed with copious amounts of deionized water and dried in a convection oven at \(60\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(12\,\mathrm{h}\).

Preparation of ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membrane: The precursor solution was prepared by dissolving 2-mIm \((\approx99\%\) , Sigma–Aldrich, \(0.25\;\mathrm{g}\) ) in methanol \((99.9\%\) , Roth, \(50\;\mathrm{mL}\) ). Consequently, the substrate covered with a \(\mathrm{ZnAl-NO}_{3}\) LDH membrane was vertically placed in a \(50\;\mathrm{mL}\) Teflon-lined stainless-steel vessel and precursor solution \((35\;\mathrm{mL})\) was poured into the vessel and sealed. The vessel was then put into a convection oven preheated to \(80\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\). After \(36\,\mathrm{h}\), the vessel was taken out and allowed to cool to room temperature in air. Finally, the membrane was removed and washed with copious amounts of deionized water. The thus prepared ZIF-8-ZnAl- \(\mathrm{NO}_{3}\) LDH composite membrane was then dried in air.

